WEBVTT

1
00:01:35.863 --> 00:01:37.615
Is it real?

2
00:01:37.906 --> 00:01:39.225
Yes.

3
00:01:39.449 --> 00:01:42.122
At least that's what my father
told my mother.

4
00:01:42.995 --> 00:01:45.225
Why do you have it?

5
00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:50.737
Your grandfather gave it to your grandmother
before he left Spain.

6
00:01:51.962 --> 00:01:55.159
She was pregnant and expecting him--

7
00:01:55.465 --> 00:01:57.535
and she never saw him again.

8
00:01:57.885 --> 00:01:59.796
It's beautiful.

9
00:02:00.054 --> 00:02:03.967
I never thought I'd touch  a real diamond.

10
00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:07.998
- Can I try it on?
- Yes.

11
00:02:15.526 --> 00:02:19.405
- It's yours now, darling.
- Really?

12
00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:25.271
I don't know. Mom always
wore it on this finger.

13
00:02:25.704 --> 00:02:28.821
She said it wasn't real.

14
00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.719
Your mother never heard the sound.

15
00:02:35.006 --> 00:02:37.042
What sound?

16
00:02:37.298 --> 00:02:39.573
The sound of the ocean.

17
00:02:41.719 --> 00:02:43.949
When I was little--

18
00:02:44.222 --> 00:02:48.010
one radio station
played the sounds of the sea.

19
00:02:50.353 --> 00:02:52.708
Giant waves.

20
00:03:03.574 --> 00:03:06.213
The sounds scared me.

21
00:03:06.493 --> 00:03:09.053
Why were you scared?

22
00:03:10.414 --> 00:03:13.451
The bottom of the sea scared me.

23
00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:20.000
All the creatures that
live there.

24
00:03:21.675 --> 00:03:23.108
Dad?

25
00:03:24.094 --> 00:03:25.652
Dad...

26
00:03:29.558 --> 00:03:32.118
Did you know that when an owl dies...

27
00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:35.878
it spits out a fur ball?

28
00:03:36.919 --> 00:03:39.922
You shouldn't go with the ponytail.
It makes you look like a fox.

29
00:03:40.615 --> 00:03:43.618
It scares away the owls.

30
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:45.960
I saw that movie.

31
00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:49.053
Don't you believe me?

32
00:03:49.225 --> 00:03:51.811
Once there was nothing here.

33
00:03:51.921 --> 00:03:54.841
Just water. Saltwater.

34
00:03:54.965 --> 00:03:57.968
Do you know what it sounded like?

35
00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.987
And the wind?

36
00:04:13.315 --> 00:04:16.318
And the two together?

37
00:05:06.887 --> 00:05:09.890
What's over there?

38
00:05:40.282 --> 00:05:42.827
When did the symptoms start?

39
00:05:42.935 --> 00:05:45.938
I don't know.
A couple of months ago.

40
00:05:50.544 --> 00:05:53.547
You can get dressed.

41
00:05:58.806 --> 00:06:01.809
Couldn't you have come sooner?

42
00:06:02.067 --> 00:06:05.070
It did not hurt as much before.

43
00:06:09.721 --> 00:06:12.682
The nurse will be by
to take some blood samples.

44
00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.813
Good morning.

45
00:06:39.681 --> 00:06:42.684
Aren't you going take it?

46
00:06:47.986 --> 00:06:50.989
Open and close your fist.

47
00:06:52.683 --> 00:06:54.935
Is that a new syringe?
- Yes.

48
00:06:55.031 --> 00:06:58.034
Is it new?
- Yes, don't worry. It's new.

49
00:07:01.423 --> 00:07:03.801
Damn!
- Sorry.

50
00:07:03.902 --> 00:07:06.905
Have you done this before?
- Your veins are just hard to find.

51
00:07:08.684 --> 00:07:11.687
Be careful.
- Sorry.

52
00:07:12.859 --> 00:07:15.821
Open and close your fist.

53
00:07:16.077 --> 00:07:19.080
Ouch! Damn!

54
00:07:19.252 --> 00:07:21.879
Give me the syringe.
- Sorry, but...

55
00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:24.951
Please
give me a syringe.

56
00:07:52.908 --> 00:07:55.911
Where did you learn that?

57
00:07:58.647 --> 00:08:01.609
Did you fast for eight hours?
-What do you mean by fast?

58
00:08:04.996 --> 00:08:07.999
Didn't they say that?
-No. They're fucking lying...

59
00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.173
Don't stab me again.

60
00:09:26.572 --> 00:09:29.575
Let's go outside now.

61
00:09:43.574 --> 00:09:46.577
Thank you.

62
00:11:52.068 --> 00:11:55.071
Why don't you leave?

63
00:11:56.112 --> 00:11:59.115
What's keeping you here?

64
00:12:16.549 --> 00:12:19.552
Did they tell you about the accident?
- Did you hear anything?

65
00:12:20.898 --> 00:12:23.817
I only heard Luis.

66
00:12:23.941 --> 00:12:26.944
The boy furthest away...
- Luis?

67
00:12:27.464 --> 00:12:30.425
Luis is doing well.
I helped him on his way.

68
00:12:32.508 --> 00:12:35.469
He told me that he repented
and asked for forgiveness...

69
00:12:37.856 --> 00:12:39.774
for stealing a watch.

70
00:12:39.639 --> 00:12:41.599
What are you talking about?

71
00:12:41.683 --> 00:12:44.644
You are a disgrace. You fool.
You come here to talk nonsense.

72
00:12:48.423 --> 00:12:50.759
My son was not a thief.
Now, let me explain. I came here because ...

73
00:12:50.858 --> 00:12:55.861
Go away! Luis, tell him to go.
Show a little respect for our son.

74
00:13:27.515 --> 00:13:29.809
Hai was asking for you.

75
00:13:29.906 --> 00:13:32.909
Tell him I'll drop by tomorrow.

76
00:13:58.519 --> 00:14:00.479
Hello.

77
00:14:00.562 --> 00:14:03.565
Dad, I tried to call you.
- Sorry, I'm a bit late. Let's go.

78
00:14:05.563 --> 00:14:08.566
Take your bag. Ready?

79
00:14:13.346 --> 00:14:16.308
Thanks, Lili.
Tomorrow at five o'clock?

80
00:14:17.956 --> 00:14:20.875
Say goodbye to Lili.

81
00:14:20.999 --> 00:14:24.002
And Li.
-Bye.

82
00:14:25.652 --> 00:14:28.655
Fish is gross.
We always eat the same thing.

83
00:14:30.827 --> 00:14:33.830
What would you prefer?

84
00:14:35.089 --> 00:14:38.092
A burger with fries...

85
00:14:40.089 --> 00:14:42.925
and a chocolate milkshake.

86
00:14:43.045 --> 00:14:46.007
With pleasure.

87
00:14:46.134 --> 00:14:48.469
And the lady?

88
00:14:48.568 --> 00:14:50.695
Fried eggs with sausages--

89
00:14:50.785 --> 00:14:53.788
and a potato frittata
with cream and cinnamon.

90
00:15:05.049 --> 00:15:08.052
Burger.

91
00:15:09.528 --> 00:15:12.489
And look at all the fries.

92
00:15:12.615 --> 00:15:15.618
French fries here,
there, and everywhere.

93
00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:21.793
And a large chocolate milkshake.

94
00:15:23.137 --> 00:15:25.431
What would you like, madam?

95
00:15:25.529 --> 00:15:28.532
Fried egg.
- Fried egg...

96
00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:31.793
With sausages.
- Sausages...

97
00:15:32.487 --> 00:15:35.490
And a potato frittata.

98
00:15:35.792 --> 00:15:38.795
Frittata...
- With cream and cinnamon.

99
00:15:45.315 --> 00:15:48.318
As ordered.

100
00:15:51.315 --> 00:15:54.318
What did you have for lunch today?
- Rice and chicken.

101
00:15:54.533 --> 00:15:56.326
Dad, did you know...

102
00:15:56.402 --> 00:15:59.405
that if an space suit
gets a hole, it explodes?

103
00:16:00.142 --> 00:16:03.145
Tomorrow, I'll ask Lili
to make something else for you.

104
00:16:04.142 --> 00:16:07.145
It isn't Lili who cooks.
- So I'll tell Jung.

105
00:16:07.621 --> 00:16:10.624
It's because of gravity.

106
00:16:13.622 --> 00:16:16.625
Stop kicking the table, Mateo.

107
00:16:23.624 --> 00:16:26.585
And don't cram all that food
in your mouth.

108
00:16:27.102 --> 00:16:30.105
I've told you a thousand times.
A thousand times.

109
00:16:34.234 --> 00:16:37.237
Don't make a mess.
Put it in your mouth again.

110
00:16:40.147 --> 00:16:43.150
Food in the mouth, Mateo.
Come on.

111
00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:47.673
Food in the mouth, right now!

112
00:16:58.628 --> 00:17:00.880
More milk?
- No.

113
00:17:05.585 --> 00:17:08.046
Stop it!

114
00:17:07.716 --> 00:17:10.719
Leave the table
and go into your room.

115
00:17:25.936 --> 00:17:28.939
I told you to go to your room,
not to rinse off your plate.

116
00:18:13.072 --> 00:18:15.741
What's wrong?

117
00:18:15.855 --> 00:18:18.858
I peed my pants.

118
00:18:19.116 --> 00:18:22.119
I'll wash them tomorrow, Dad.

119
00:19:41.214 --> 00:19:44.217
Yes?

120
00:19:45.301 --> 00:19:48.179
Just a moment.

121
00:19:48.301 --> 00:19:50.678
Can you turn it down a bit?

122
00:19:50.779 --> 00:19:53.782
Turn down the music and stop singing.

123
00:19:59.128 --> 00:20:02.131
Yes, I'm here.
Sorry about that.

124
00:20:02.912 --> 00:20:05.915
Yes, the cemetery called again.

125
00:20:07.434 --> 00:20:10.437
No, they're going to build a mall.

126
00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:14.133
Right on top of Dad.

127
00:20:14.305 --> 00:20:17.183
They have offered me money.

128
00:20:17.305 --> 00:20:20.308
Good money.

129
00:20:20.653 --> 00:20:23.656
They handle the coffin and everything.

130
00:20:27.828 --> 00:20:30.372
It's a good deal.

131
00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:33.483
There's no way to prevent it, anyway.

132
00:20:36.351 --> 00:20:39.354
We should definitely have Dad cremated.

133
00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:44.379
Okay, let's do it.

134
00:20:44.482 --> 00:20:47.485
Yeah, okay. I'll call you.

135
00:20:48.178 --> 00:20:49.972
Okay, next week.

136
00:20:50.787 --> 00:20:52.372
Take care.

137
00:20:51.831 --> 00:20:54.834
See you.

138
00:20:56.919 --> 00:20:59.338
Who's being cremated?
- No one.

139
00:20:59.441 --> 00:21:02.444
Don't lie.

140
00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:09.923
I'll give you a Thai massage.

141
00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:13.751
Who?

142
00:21:16.529 --> 00:21:19.532
If you don't tell me...
- My father!

143
00:21:20.617 --> 00:21:23.620
He's going to be cremated.

144
00:21:25.749 --> 00:21:28.752
Which of you takes after him the most?
- I don't know.

145
00:21:29.227 --> 00:21:32.230
I don't remember what he looked like.

146
00:21:39.446 --> 00:21:42.115
Give me a kiss.

147
00:21:42.229 --> 00:21:45.232
I want to go.

148
00:21:45.403 --> 00:21:48.364
I'm gonna go now.

149
00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:52.363
Stop, I'm leaving.
What the hell are you doing?

150
00:22:09.797 --> 00:22:12.758
Asshole.

151
00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:18.453
Crazy.

152
00:22:53.542 --> 00:22:56.545
Where are the others?
I met Chinaza on the way here.

153
00:22:58.021 --> 00:23:00.773
Where?
- In El Fondo.

154
00:23:00.890 --> 00:23:03.768
I sent the idiot away.

155
00:23:03.891 --> 00:23:06.894
Where are Cheikh and Mamadou?

156
00:23:07.109 --> 00:23:09.695
Keep them under control, or we're screwed!

157
00:23:09.805 --> 00:23:12.808
I told you, they can't sell here.
It's off limits.

158
00:23:14.979 --> 00:23:17.982
Understood?
Do you understand what I'm saying?

159
00:23:18.458 --> 00:23:21.461
Elsewhere, no one buys.

160
00:23:21.589 --> 00:23:24.592
I also hear
you've started selling drugs.

161
00:23:31.242 --> 00:23:34.203
Pack up, guys. They're coming.

162
00:23:35.243 --> 00:23:38.788
Watch out for cops.
Run!

163
00:23:39.417 --> 00:23:42.378
I have something to show you.
At home with me.

164
00:23:42.548 --> 00:23:45.551
in your home? Jeez...

165
00:23:55.027 --> 00:23:56.988
It's stuck.

166
00:23:57.072 --> 00:24:00.075
Won't open.

167
00:24:01.942 --> 00:24:03.694
Thank you, Ige.

168
00:24:03.768 --> 00:24:06.771
It's no use lowering the price
if nobody wants them.

169
00:24:08.203 --> 00:24:10.997
Are they all like that?

170
00:24:11.116 --> 00:24:14.119
Most of them.

171
00:24:14.943 --> 00:24:17.946
It's been a lousy month.
You have to talk to the Chinese.

172
00:24:19.509 --> 00:24:22.512
Maybe I can get umbrellas.

173
00:24:23.639 --> 00:24:26.642
Screw that!
It never rains here.

174
00:24:26.902 --> 00:24:29.905
Yes, it rains.

175
00:24:33.163 --> 00:24:36.166
Can you sleep, with the baby?
- No none can.

176
00:24:36.815 --> 00:24:39.818
Keep it down, will you. I have a guest.

177
00:24:43.165 --> 00:24:46.168
Who made this?
Was it you?

178
00:24:47.469 --> 00:24:50.472
Who made this shit? Would you
even use such a shit bag?

179
00:25:01.992 --> 00:25:04.995
We make no money faking these goods.
It's now or never.

180
00:25:06.994 --> 00:25:09.997
20 construction workers
at 1300 euros each...

181
00:25:11.168 --> 00:25:13.795
That's a lot of money.

182
00:25:13.907 --> 00:25:16.910
I have to think about it first.
- Why? We think too much.

183
00:25:17.777 --> 00:25:19.738
We'll lose the contract with Mendoza.

184
00:25:19.821 --> 00:25:22.824
What about the workers? Should they
keep on making this shit?

185
00:25:25.039 --> 00:25:29.293
I don't know what you are saying,
but you have to do something quickly.

186
00:25:29.256 --> 00:25:32.259
I can't continue selling crap.

187
00:25:34.388 --> 00:25:37.391
The idiot must be good for something.
- That idiot has done far more than you.

188
00:25:50.347 --> 00:25:53.350
For your friend in the police.

189
00:25:54.869 --> 00:25:57.163
Have you talked to Mendoza?

190
00:25:57.261 --> 00:26:00.264
Yes. My brother has a contact at
a building site in Badalona.

191
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:04.003
They need lots of workers.
How much is this?

192
00:26:07.262 --> 00:26:10.265
How much?

193
00:26:10.784 --> 00:26:13.787
It's no laughing matter, Hai.
How much is it?

194
00:26:15.741 --> 00:26:18.744
What's wrong with you? It's a
sensitive issue, and I have a family.

195
00:26:20.133 --> 00:26:22.469
We aren't at home in China.

196
00:26:22.568 --> 00:26:25.571
Thanks, I know.

197
00:26:28.656 --> 00:26:31.659
Why did you come here then?

198
00:26:33.352 --> 00:26:36.355
Because I love you.

199
00:26:46.919 --> 00:26:49.922
You're a strong man.

200
00:26:50.050 --> 00:26:53.053
An important man.

201
00:26:53.311 --> 00:26:56.314
Do you love me?

202
00:27:21.663 --> 00:27:24.666
Say you love me.
I know you love me.

203
00:27:27.706 --> 00:27:30.709
How many times have I told you.
Am I speaking Chinese?

204
00:27:31.577 --> 00:27:36.456
I have explained it to them ...
- They can't sell here, Uxbal.

205
00:27:35.795 --> 00:27:38.798
You'd better fucking learn
to speak African.

206
00:27:40.316 --> 00:27:45.319
You should also talk to your people
and get them to calm down.

207
00:27:47.056 --> 00:27:50.059
That's what I pay you for.

208
00:27:51.970 --> 00:27:54.973
Listen, Uxbal. We've known each other
for quite a while now.

209
00:27:56.362 --> 00:27:59.365
But next time you screw up you
you're done.

210
00:28:00.145 --> 00:28:03.148
Clear?

211
00:28:03.363 --> 00:28:06.366
Is that clear?

212
00:28:08.625 --> 00:28:11.628
Okay, moving on...

213
00:28:16.626 --> 00:28:19.629
October and November.

214
00:28:20.061 --> 00:28:23.064
Next time they pay late,
they're fucked.

215
00:28:23.975 --> 00:28:26.978
Clear?
Or should I translate?

216
00:29:26.156 --> 00:29:29.159
Daddy's home!
- Mom picked us up from school barefoot.

217
00:29:29.374 --> 00:29:32.085
I took my shoes off too.

218
00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:34.911
Well?
- Well what?

219
00:29:35.027 --> 00:29:38.030
Why weren't you home?
- I can't be in two places at once.

220
00:29:38.810 --> 00:29:41.771
Mom's making spaghetti.

221
00:29:42.027 --> 00:29:44.738
Turn off the TV.

222
00:29:44.854 --> 00:29:47.607
Sit down and eat.

223
00:29:47.724 --> 00:29:50.727
Why is the shower on?

224
00:29:53.637 --> 00:29:56.640
None of your shirts was ironed.
Neat way to iron, huh?

225
00:30:15.727 --> 00:30:17.270
Coming to eat?

226
00:30:17.336 --> 00:30:19.380
Lili called, she was worried.

227
00:30:19.467 --> 00:30:22.428
We agreed that you would call
if you wanted to pick up the kids.

228
00:30:22.554 --> 00:30:25.516
Sorry, but a client canceled.

229
00:30:25.816 --> 00:30:28.819
Then call my cell!

230
00:30:36.643 --> 00:30:39.646
Want some frittata?
It has apple in it.

231
00:30:39.774 --> 00:30:42.777
It's like a potato frittata, but juicier,
and sweet. I bought it from Miguel.

232
00:30:45.427 --> 00:30:48.430
Won't you eat something?
- No, I'm not hungry, honey.

233
00:30:50.471 --> 00:30:53.474
Miguel's daughter told me
that they were out driving...

234
00:30:53.950 --> 00:30:56.786
yesterday, when a motorbike cut them off
like a goddamned maniac.

235
00:30:56.906 --> 00:30:59.659
So Miguel yelled: "Die, you idiot!"

236
00:30:59.777 --> 00:31:02.446
Five minutes later, they saw the
bike lying on the road--

237
00:31:02.559 --> 00:31:05.562
and the rider was completely crushed
in a pool of blood.

238
00:31:05.820 --> 00:31:08.823
Miguel was so shaken
that he drove to the hospital.

239
00:31:09.430 --> 00:31:12.433
I don't get why he was shocked. If anyone
did something like that to me...

240
00:31:13.083 --> 00:31:16.086
Quiet, Maramba, enough already.

241
00:31:18.431 --> 00:31:21.434
If you could stop talking,
maybe you'd get hungry.

242
00:31:23.345 --> 00:31:25.430
Please put out your cigarette.

243
00:31:26.736 --> 00:31:29.572
And take your foot off the table
while were eating.

244
00:31:34.390 --> 00:31:37.393
Do you want to stay
and watch a movie, Mom?

245
00:31:43.390 --> 00:31:46.393
It's late, sweetie.

246
00:31:47.739 --> 00:31:50.742
If I don't say anything, how can I get you
to stop taking them to funerals?

247
00:31:52.652 --> 00:31:55.280
Telepathy? That's why Mateo still
wets the bed.

248
00:31:55.392 --> 00:31:56.810
I haven't taken them in a long time.

249
00:31:56.871 --> 00:31:59.874
That's not what they say.
Just because you have custody...

250
00:32:00.262 --> 00:32:03.265
Are you here to see the children,
or to interrogate them?

251
00:32:07.481 --> 00:32:10.484
Mom, the spaghetti's tasteless.

252
00:32:12.873 --> 00:32:15.876
You almost finished it anyway.
- Go.

253
00:32:17.134 --> 00:32:20.137
Leave now.
Let us eat in peace.

254
00:32:22.439 --> 00:32:25.442
I'd better go.

255
00:32:26.440 --> 00:32:29.443
See you, sweetheart.

256
00:32:30.657 --> 00:32:33.660
Be good, sweetheart.

257
00:33:09.532 --> 00:33:12.493
Marambra...

258
00:33:14.402 --> 00:33:17.321
Sorry. You did good.

259
00:33:17.445 --> 00:33:19.156
I did good?
- Yes.

260
00:33:19.229 --> 00:33:22.232
I don't need your praise.
I'm not a dog.

261
00:33:22.621 --> 00:33:25.624
You turned the kids against me.
- No, Maramba, you do that yourself.

262
00:33:27.142 --> 00:33:30.104
It's like it bothers you
to see me happy.

263
00:33:30.230 --> 00:33:33.233
It's only with you that I find it hard
to be myself, and feel good.

264
00:33:33.404 --> 00:33:36.407
Do you remember what happened
the last time you felt good?

265
00:33:37.405 --> 00:33:40.408
Should I remind you?

266
00:33:41.057 --> 00:33:44.060
You don't need to remind me.

267
00:33:46.232 --> 00:33:49.194
Why are you laughing?

268
00:33:52.972 --> 00:33:55.975
At least I laugh.
And I like seeing people smile.

269
00:33:57.538 --> 00:34:00.541
I'm happy if I'm happy
and depressed if I'm depressed.

270
00:34:05.887 --> 00:34:08.890
I just wanted to...

271
00:34:10.366 --> 00:34:12.952
I love you.

272
00:34:13.062 --> 00:34:16.065
I love you, I said.

273
00:34:25.281 --> 00:34:28.284
Yes, me too.

274
00:34:54.197 --> 00:34:57.200
You don't have any money on you?

275
00:35:09.721 --> 00:35:12.432
A little more?
- No.

276
00:35:12.548 --> 00:35:15.551
Maybe, now that you're selling the grave...
- Who told you that?

277
00:35:22.548 --> 00:35:25.551
Tito.
- When did you see him?

278
00:35:27.027 --> 00:35:29.989
Don't start, please. I gave him
a massage. He had a sore lower back.

279
00:35:38.594 --> 00:35:41.597
It's not a grave, it's a niche.

280
00:36:13.250 --> 00:36:15.044
But...

281
00:36:15.120 --> 00:36:18.123
Nobody told me to fast.

282
00:36:21.295 --> 00:36:23.213
Maybe...

283
00:36:24.730 --> 00:36:25.773
it threw off the results.

284
00:36:25.817 --> 00:36:28.820
No, sorry.
Fasting is merely a formality.

285
00:36:31.862 --> 00:36:34.865
What now?
- Excuse me?

286
00:36:35.862 --> 00:36:38.239
How...

287
00:36:38.340 --> 00:36:41.218
I would like to know
what's going to happen.

288
00:36:41.341 --> 00:36:44.302
It depends on how your body
responds to chemotherapy.

289
00:36:44.690 --> 00:36:47.693
In your case,
it's been so long--

290
00:36:47.993 --> 00:36:52.996
that it has metastasized from
prostate to bone and liver.

291
00:36:54.951 --> 00:36:56.536
Which means...

292
00:36:56.604 --> 00:36:59.565
But how long?
Roughly how long?

293
00:37:05.257 --> 00:37:08.260
With medical treatment
we can maintain your quality of life--

294
00:37:09.127 --> 00:37:12.130
for a few months.

295
00:37:16.084 --> 00:37:19.087
Months?

296
00:38:19.135 --> 00:38:22.138
Dad, I learned a trick.

297
00:38:22.745 --> 00:38:25.414
Think of a country
that starts with D.

298
00:38:25.527 --> 00:38:27.738
Dad, look at me.

299
00:38:27.833 --> 00:38:29.793
Ready?
- Yes.

300
00:38:29.876 --> 00:38:32.879
Now think of an animal
that starts with I.

301
00:38:33.529 --> 00:38:35.197
Hippopotamus doesn't start with I.

302
00:38:36.964 --> 00:38:38.632
Are you ready?
- Yes.

303
00:38:39.573 --> 00:38:42.576
You're guaranteed to be thinking
of iguana and Denmark.

304
00:38:47.139 --> 00:38:50.142
How'd you know?

305
00:38:50.662 --> 00:38:53.623
Dad, how do you spell
"beautiful"?

306
00:38:53.749 --> 00:38:56.752
Just the way it sounds.
- As in?

307
00:38:58.793 --> 00:39:01.755
Biu-ti-ful.

308
00:42:42.038 --> 00:42:45.041
No, it's nothing, don't worry.

309
00:42:45.255 --> 00:42:48.258
Just get the kids,
and take them home to your place.

310
00:42:50.561 --> 00:42:53.063
I don't know.

311
00:42:53.170 --> 00:42:56.173
Until I'm released.
In a couple of days, probably.

312
00:43:15.912 --> 00:43:18.915
Times are hard.

313
00:43:21.000 --> 00:43:24.003
We'll stop making bags
and copying movies.

314
00:43:26.087 --> 00:43:29.090
You were right.

315
00:43:30.088 --> 00:43:32.549
Construction is good business.

316
00:43:32.654 --> 00:43:35.657
The laborers will keep working
for Mendoza.

317
00:43:36.610 --> 00:43:39.613
Pay them what we agreed.

318
00:43:42.263 --> 00:43:45.266
You won't regret it.
We lend a helping hand...

319
00:43:47.002 --> 00:43:50.005
and it's safer for us, too.
Do you understand? There's lots of money to be made.

320
00:43:52.699 --> 00:43:55.702
Uxbal asked me for money
for heaters in the warehouse.

321
00:43:57.396 --> 00:44:00.399
People shouldn't freeze in the basement.

322
00:44:01.135 --> 00:44:04.096
Okay, I'll see what I can do.
Where are you going?

323
00:44:05.483 --> 00:44:08.486
I gotta go home.

324
00:44:35.791 --> 00:44:38.794
You came to blows
over to a negro?

325
00:44:43.271 --> 00:44:46.274
How much was bail?

326
00:44:46.619 --> 00:44:49.622
I'll pay it back,
as fast as I can.

327
00:44:51.663 --> 00:44:57.001
Never mind. I'll take it from the money
we get for Dad's niche.

328
00:44:56.533 --> 00:44:58.869
It's all set?

329
00:44:58.969 --> 00:45:01.972
We just sign the papers
from the cemetery, and we get the money.

330
00:45:03.708 --> 00:45:06.711
But first we have to cremate him.
Then we do what we want.

331
00:45:07.360 --> 00:45:10.322
We can bury him in the urn with
Mom's ashes, and save money.

332
00:45:10.448 --> 00:45:13.451
Have a look at these.

333
00:45:14.405 --> 00:45:17.408
Careful, it's Dad's papers.

334
00:45:21.319 --> 00:45:24.322
How are the Chinese at the site?

335
00:45:26.624 --> 00:45:29.627
Mendoza's freaking out.

336
00:45:30.015 --> 00:45:32.309
Most of them don't know
a damn thing about construction.

337
00:45:32.407 --> 00:45:35.410
None of them speaks Spanish,
and they all look like alike.

338
00:45:37.712 --> 00:45:40.006
Did you tell Marambra
about the cemetery?

339
00:45:40.104 --> 00:45:42.356
No.

340
00:45:42.452 --> 00:45:45.163
Well...

341
00:45:45.278 --> 00:45:49.281
She called me a while ago. She called
trying to get a hold of you, or something...

342
00:45:50.322 --> 00:45:53.325
but I didn't tell her anything.
I haven't seen her in a long time.

343
00:46:37.242 --> 00:46:40.245
Uxbal.

344
00:46:44.068 --> 00:46:47.029
Take it.

345
00:46:47.199 --> 00:46:50.202
It's not necessary.
- I need to know what my son said.

346
00:46:51.374 --> 00:46:54.377
The day before the accident
we'd quarreled.

347
00:46:57.852 --> 00:47:00.855
It's the last thing I...

348
00:47:01.679 --> 00:47:04.682
Your son died in peace.
He was scared so I helped him.

349
00:47:07.419 --> 00:47:10.422
He told me
where he had hidden your watch.

350
00:47:12.158 --> 00:47:13.577
Where?

351
00:47:13.638 --> 00:47:16.641
Behind a leg, under his bed.

352
00:47:19.333 --> 00:47:22.336
Yes.

353
00:47:28.987 --> 00:47:31.990
I'm terribly sorry. Really.

354
00:47:57.338 --> 00:48:00.300
Who is it?
- It's me.

355
00:48:05.340 --> 00:48:08.176
I thought you were coming by tomorrow.
- I was nearby, so...

356
00:48:08.296 --> 00:48:10.423
Come in.

357
00:48:10.514 --> 00:48:13.517
Thanks for helping with the kids.
I can take them now...

358
00:48:14.079 --> 00:48:16.415
Quiet.

359
00:48:16.515 --> 00:48:19.518
The kids are sleeping.
- What did you tell them?

360
00:48:20.167 --> 00:48:23.170
That you were with your brother.
That it was something to do with work.

361
00:48:29.343 --> 00:48:32.346
I'll get them tomorrow
before they leave for school, okay?

362
00:48:34.256 --> 00:48:36.300
You're welcome to stay here.

363
00:48:36.387 --> 00:48:39.098
I can make coffee or tea.

364
00:48:39.214 --> 00:48:41.841
There's also wine.

365
00:48:41.952 --> 00:48:44.955
Don't look at me like that.
I swear, I haven't started drinking.

366
00:48:47.779 --> 00:48:50.782
I opened the bottle for a friend.
You remember Laura?

367
00:50:02.832 --> 00:50:05.126
Here you go.

368
00:50:05.224 --> 00:50:08.227
Thank you.

369
00:50:13.443 --> 00:50:16.446
Did they hurt you?
- No, I'm okay.

370
00:50:20.009 --> 00:50:23.012
Ana told me about something
she'd dreamed.

371
00:50:23.835 --> 00:50:27.838
You came home to the apartment,
and the bedroom was filled with sand.

372
00:50:29.836 --> 00:50:32.839
Like a dune, which piled up
almost to the ceiling.

373
00:50:33.923 --> 00:50:36.926
You climbed on top and began to dig...
- I'm leaving.

374
00:50:37.923 --> 00:50:40.926
I asked her where Mateo was.

375
00:50:43.273 --> 00:50:46.276
She didn't know...

376
00:50:46.534 --> 00:50:49.537
but she thought
he lay buried under the sand.

377
00:50:50.708 --> 00:50:53.711
Why are you leaving?

378
00:50:53.882 --> 00:50:56.885
Stay here.

379
00:51:05.710 --> 00:51:08.713
I think
you will look at me differently.

380
00:51:10.014 --> 00:51:13.017
It's probably not a good idea.

381
00:51:13.407 --> 00:51:16.410
We both know what will happen.
- There is room for all of us here.

382
00:51:16.841 --> 00:51:18.760
You can see the ocean from the kitchen.

383
00:51:18.842 --> 00:51:21.845
Then we'll have breakfast together,
like in the old days.

384
00:51:21.991 --> 00:51:24.978
I'll make you toast with eggs...

385
00:51:25.321 --> 00:51:28.324
Be quiet for a moment.
- The children need me.

386
00:51:30.147 --> 00:51:33.150
They can't wake up to a
different father every weekend.

387
00:51:33.452 --> 00:51:35.538
Always dredging up that crap.

388
00:51:35.627 --> 00:51:38.630
It's not just about the kids.
I need you.

389
00:51:39.105 --> 00:51:42.108
I haven't relapsed once
in five months.

390
00:51:42.671 --> 00:51:45.674
Give me a chance, my love.

391
00:51:47.498 --> 00:51:49.583
You've said the same thing
so many times.

392
00:51:49.671 --> 00:51:52.674
I haven't been manic for a long time.
I'm different now, I promise.

393
00:51:54.238 --> 00:51:55.989
Are you taking your pills?

394
00:51:56.063 --> 00:51:59.025
You told me to stop taking them,
when I was breastfeeding Mateo.

395
00:51:59.151 --> 00:52:02.029
You're obsessed with those damn pills!

396
00:52:02.152 --> 00:52:04.863
The doctor said that you should...

397
00:52:04.978 --> 00:52:07.981
The doctor would say anything
to get rid of me.

398
00:52:08.935 --> 00:52:11.938
None of that shit can cure
my manic depression.

399
00:52:15.197 --> 00:52:18.200
Now I'm trying with a light box.
- With what?

400
00:52:18.588 --> 00:52:21.591
Phototherapy. It's fantastic.

401
00:52:22.285 --> 00:52:25.288
And much cheaper than medicine.
Want to see it?

402
00:52:42.591 --> 00:52:45.594
See?

403
00:52:47.200 --> 00:52:49.661
Isn't it amazing?

404
00:52:49.766 --> 00:52:52.769
I started a couple of months ago.

405
00:52:54.593 --> 00:52:57.596
I feel wonderful.
But not like before.

406
00:52:58.637 --> 00:53:01.640
It's different now.
I feel normal,

407
00:53:02.203 --> 00:53:05.206
like everyone else.

408
00:53:54.731 --> 00:53:57.734
No, stop...

409
00:54:01.688 --> 00:54:04.024
Stop Marambra...

410
00:54:04.124 --> 00:54:07.127
Please.

411
00:54:12.038 --> 00:54:14.957
It doesn't matter.

412
00:54:15.081 --> 00:54:18.042
You're very tired.

413
00:54:18.256 --> 00:54:22.059
And I'm getting old.
- You're not; what are you talking about?

414
00:54:24.517 --> 00:54:27.520
About me.
Away, at the police station,

415
00:54:29.692 --> 00:54:32.695
I couldn't stop thinking about...

416
00:54:33.736 --> 00:54:36.739
getting back to you
and the kids gain.

417
00:54:42.737 --> 00:54:45.740
The kids and I need...

418
00:54:50.824 --> 00:54:53.827
Do you remember when we
fucked in the small closet?

419
00:54:56.565 --> 00:54:59.568
I'd just arrived in Barcelona, and
you visited me at work--the dry cleaner's.

420
00:55:00.609 --> 00:55:03.612
You took me in the closet.

421
00:55:04.479 --> 00:55:07.482
And then the owner came
and found us...

422
00:55:56.007 --> 00:55:59.010
Get up!

423
00:56:00.355 --> 00:56:03.358
It's half past seven.
There is bread and tea outside.

424
00:56:05.356 --> 00:56:08.359
Come on!

425
00:56:42.056 --> 00:56:44.684
I always find myself
in all kinds of crap.

426
00:56:44.795 --> 00:56:47.798
There are four minors.
I don't pay in advance.

427
00:56:48.579 --> 00:56:51.582
If we are inspected, where do I
hide so many damn Chinese?

428
00:56:51.884 --> 00:56:53.385
It's our only condition, Mendoza.

429
00:56:53.449 --> 00:56:56.452
I don't pay a thing until I know
whether they're worth anything.

430
00:56:57.537 --> 00:57:00.331
That's normal practice.
Right, Uxbal?

431
00:57:00.450 --> 00:57:01.493
One week's probation.

432
00:57:01.537 --> 00:57:04.456
Half of them are sick and frozen.

433
00:57:04.580 --> 00:57:07.417
They have never ever seen a drill before
in their lives.

434
00:57:07.538 --> 00:57:10.541
That doesn't exactly help
to cut costs.

435
00:57:10.972 --> 00:57:13.433
Costs...

436
00:57:13.538 --> 00:57:16.541
Okay.

437
00:57:17.235 --> 00:57:20.238
The alternative is to hire
unionized construction workers.

438
00:57:21.974 --> 00:57:24.977
Once you've crunched the numbers,
call me.

439
00:57:36.323 --> 00:57:39.326
When do you need the money?
- About a week from today.

440
00:57:41.064 --> 00:57:44.067
Stop looking like a scared Chinaman.
I'll pay next week.

441
00:57:44.977 --> 00:57:47.772
But then I need the papers
no later than Friday.

442
00:57:47.890 --> 00:57:49.850
Okay, okay.

443
00:57:49.934 --> 00:57:52.687
It's a deal.
- Good.

444
00:57:52.804 --> 00:57:55.807
How long are we here for?

445
00:57:56.109 --> 00:57:59.112
I don't know.
A couple of days.

446
00:58:00.109 --> 00:58:02.820
Can I invite Lili?

447
00:58:02.936 --> 00:58:05.939
It's too hard.
I can't take it anymore.

448
00:58:10.720 --> 00:58:13.723
It smells horrible.

449
00:58:15.938 --> 00:58:18.941
Maybe I should throw out the fish.
It's been thawed out again and again.

450
00:58:21.068 --> 00:58:24.071
Don't touch the fridge when you're barefoot.
Especially if the floor is wet.

451
00:58:26.069 --> 00:58:28.988
The power comes and goes.

452
00:58:29.112 --> 00:58:30.948
The stairs are tough, right?

453
00:58:31.027 --> 00:58:33.863
The neighbor's wife says that the stairs
helped her with her belly.

454
00:58:33.983 --> 00:58:36.986
As if I couldn't see she'd had surgery
done. They cut her belly--

455
00:58:38.027 --> 00:58:40.279
and pulled the skin so high,
her navel ended way up there.

456
00:58:40.375 --> 00:58:43.378
The doctor had to make
her a fake belly button.

457
00:58:44.898 --> 00:58:46.399
God...

458
00:58:46.463 --> 00:58:49.466
Too bad there's no electricity,
after I just bought ice cream.

459
00:58:49.854 --> 00:58:52.857
Have you tasted the mango? It's
wonderful. There's also chocolate.

460
00:58:54.595 --> 00:58:55.929
Ana, get spoons.

461
00:58:55.986 --> 00:58:58.989
Let's see. I bought you one
with chocolate chip cookies in it.

462
00:59:02.812 --> 00:59:05.440
It melted.
- It tastes better that way.

463
00:59:05.552 --> 00:59:08.555
Yummy.

464
00:59:09.205 --> 00:59:12.208
Here.

465
00:59:13.206 --> 00:59:16.209
Is that chocolate?

466
00:59:20.946 --> 00:59:23.949
Don't be gross.

467
00:59:25.250 --> 00:59:26.209
Careful.

468
00:59:26.250 --> 00:59:29.253
Should we take a trip to the countryside
for Ana's birthday?

469
00:59:29.946 --> 00:59:32.741
Just a weekend or a Saturday.

470
00:59:32.860 --> 00:59:35.446
Sure. Where?
- I don't know.

471
00:59:35.556 --> 00:59:38.183
The Pyrenees?
The kids have never seen snow.

472
00:59:38.295 --> 00:59:40.548
They have never been
outside this neighborhood.

473
00:59:40.644 --> 00:59:43.188
We can go camping.
One of my friends went.

474
00:59:43.296 --> 00:59:46.299
No, I'd rather have a dog. A small one.

475
00:59:47.296 --> 00:59:50.299
No, honey. They shit all day long
and cost a fortune.

476
00:59:51.166 --> 00:59:54.127
Getting away is much more fun.
Let me try some.

477
00:59:54.254 --> 00:59:57.257
I have to try it.

478
00:59:58.472 --> 01:00:01.475
What are you doing, Marambra?
- Want a taste?

479
01:00:01.603 --> 01:00:04.606
Use the spoon. Don't be so...
You are so disgusting.

480
01:00:05.516 --> 01:00:08.519
Good, huh?
- Want to try it?

481
01:00:08.821 --> 01:00:10.823
Go for it.

482
01:00:10.909 --> 01:00:12.619
Stick your fingers in there.

483
01:00:12.691 --> 01:00:15.569
Come on.

484
01:00:15.692 --> 01:00:18.695
Good, right?
- Give it a rest.

485
01:00:22.909 --> 01:00:25.912
You're one to talk. Don't you
remember how you proposed to me?

486
01:00:27.519 --> 01:00:29.104
What did he do?

487
01:00:29.171 --> 01:00:32.174
If you're telling the story,
tell about how you gazed at me.

488
01:00:33.607 --> 01:00:36.610
You and your gazes.
I hadn't even seen you.

489
01:00:36.825 --> 01:00:39.828
Hadn't even seen me?
- I'm the one telling the story, not you.

490
01:00:41.564 --> 01:00:44.567
The day I met your father
at a party, he said--

491
01:00:45.087 --> 01:00:48.090
that I had the most beautiful nose
he had ever seen.

492
01:00:49.739 --> 01:00:52.492
And, of course, I believed him.

493
01:00:52.609 --> 01:00:55.612
Then he took my hand
to read my palm.

494
01:00:56.871 --> 01:00:59.874
He said I'd get married
to an insufferable man--

495
01:01:00.741 --> 01:01:03.201
but I would be loved very much.

496
01:01:03.306 --> 01:01:06.309
Who knows how many girls he'd tried
that on, but it worked on me.

497
01:01:07.350 --> 01:01:10.353
He said if I let go of his hand,
it wouldn't come true.

498
01:01:11.438 --> 01:01:14.399
And all of a sudden,
before I knew what was happening--

499
01:01:14.525 --> 01:01:17.486
he lifted my hand
up to his nose--

500
01:01:18.743 --> 01:01:21.746
and stuck my finger in his nostril.

501
01:01:23.178 --> 01:01:25.681
He picked a booger
and put it in my hand--

502
01:01:25.788 --> 01:01:28.749
so I would always carry
a part of him with me.

503
01:01:29.614 --> 01:01:32.617
A black, hairy snot.
It was disgusting.

504
01:01:33.658 --> 01:01:35.702
So you shouldn't say anything.

505
01:01:35.789 --> 01:01:38.792
It's not true. Do you think I could've
thought of something like that?

506
01:02:28.404 --> 01:02:30.364
What do you want?

507
01:02:30.447 --> 01:02:33.450
Did you come to apologize?

508
01:02:37.057 --> 01:02:40.018
Money?
Don't give me fucking money.

509
01:02:40.753 --> 01:02:43.088
Apologize to them too.

510
01:02:43.188 --> 01:02:46.191
Just seeing you...
If you didn't have kids, I'd kill you.

511
01:02:47.666 --> 01:02:49.794
They knew what they were doing.

512
01:02:49.885 --> 01:02:52.888
They didn't have residence permits,
and they sold drugs.

513
01:02:53.363 --> 01:02:56.366
Ekweme and the others knew
they couldn't be here.

514
01:02:56.886 --> 01:02:59.221
The police won't allow it.

515
01:02:59.320 --> 01:03:02.073
Do you understand?

516
01:03:02.190 --> 01:03:05.193
Take the damn money.

517
01:03:07.365 --> 01:03:10.368
What about me?
What should I do with my child?

518
01:03:12.496 --> 01:03:15.499
I don't know, Ige. I don't know.

519
01:05:44.080 --> 01:05:47.083
Here. Drink this.

520
01:05:54.430 --> 01:05:56.432
How's your wife?

521
01:05:56.517 --> 01:05:59.019
Fine. Better.

522
01:05:59.125 --> 01:06:02.128
And the kids?
- They're doing well.

523
01:06:03.083 --> 01:06:05.293
And you?

524
01:06:05.387 --> 01:06:08.390
You're dying.

525
01:06:08.866 --> 01:06:11.202
So it seems.

526
01:06:13.997 --> 01:06:15.915
Spit.

527
01:06:26.651 --> 01:06:28.778
Have you taken stock of your life?

528
01:06:28.869 --> 01:06:31.872
Are you ready to say goodbye?

529
01:06:32.564 --> 01:06:35.567
Yes, I think so.
I'm working on it.

530
01:06:36.174 --> 01:06:39.177
You think so?
You need to be sure.

531
01:06:39.523 --> 01:06:42.317
Take control of your life.
Don't leave any loose ends.

532
01:06:42.435 --> 01:06:45.438
I don't want to die, Bea.

533
01:06:46.784 --> 01:06:49.787
I'm afraid
to leave the kids in the lurch.

534
01:06:50.480 --> 01:06:53.483
Do you think you're the one
looking after the kids?

535
01:06:54.002 --> 01:06:56.964
Don't be naive, Uxbal.
The universe will provide for them.

536
01:06:57.090 --> 01:07:00.093
Yes, but the universe
doesn't pay the rent.

537
01:07:04.047 --> 01:07:06.758
When I was on Ana's age--

538
01:07:06.873 --> 01:07:09.876
my mother died.
I barely remember her.

539
01:07:10.483 --> 01:07:13.486
My father died without me
ever meeting him.

540
01:07:15.787 --> 01:07:18.123
I don't want that for my children.

541
01:07:18.223 --> 01:07:21.226
Then tell them that.
Tell them everything.

542
01:07:22.267 --> 01:07:25.270
The dead will never be at peace
if they are in debt to the living.

543
01:07:26.006 --> 01:07:29.009
Why is this happening to me?
Am I being punished?

544
01:07:30.876 --> 01:07:33.087
You can pack up and go--

545
01:07:33.181 --> 01:07:36.184
or hang in there, like fools do.

546
01:07:36.964 --> 01:07:39.258
It's a long hard road, Uxbal.

547
01:07:39.355 --> 01:07:42.358
Death is not the end of everything,
you know that.

548
01:07:43.443 --> 01:07:46.321
I won't die, Bea.

549
01:07:46.444 --> 01:07:49.447
No.

550
01:07:51.314 --> 01:07:54.317
No.

551
01:07:58.663 --> 01:08:01.666
Yes, you'll die.

552
01:08:02.663 --> 01:08:05.666
I see it,
and there's nothing I can do about it.

553
01:08:06.881 --> 01:08:09.842
Get your affairs in order, Uxbal.
It's all that matters.

554
01:08:12.969 --> 01:08:15.972
Chemotherapy is poison.

555
01:08:28.275 --> 01:08:30.819
What did you eat for breakfast?

556
01:08:30.927 --> 01:08:33.930
Coffee with milk.

557
01:08:37.755 --> 01:08:40.758
You've always been such a sweet boy.

558
01:08:41.363 --> 01:08:44.366
Remember what I said the day we met?

559
01:08:44.712 --> 01:08:47.715
That we got our gift for free--

560
01:08:48.495 --> 01:08:51.498
and we must pass it on likewise.

561
01:08:58.061 --> 01:08:59.521
Here.

562
01:08:59.583 --> 01:09:02.127
Give this to the kids when needed.

563
01:09:02.235 --> 01:09:05.113
What is it?
- Protection.

564
01:09:05.236 --> 01:09:07.864
When you must leave them--

565
01:09:07.975 --> 01:09:10.936
give each of them one.

566
01:09:34.457 --> 01:09:37.419
He said he felt
like a muddy sea inside.

567
01:09:38.675 --> 01:09:41.636
That his eyes felt like jelly,

568
01:09:41.762 --> 01:09:44.765
and his hair was on fire.

569
01:10:31.420 --> 01:10:34.423
Get up. It's half past seven.

570
01:10:51.293 --> 01:10:54.296
How many heaters did Uxbal bring?
- Six.

571
01:11:05.685 --> 01:11:07.854
How's Ana?

572
01:11:07.947 --> 01:11:09.908
Hi, Lili.

573
01:11:09.991 --> 01:11:12.827
How are you?

574
01:11:12.948 --> 01:11:15.951
The heaters will make sure
that you don't freeze.

575
01:11:17.035 --> 01:11:19.329
Ana's fine.
She wants to see you.

576
01:11:19.426 --> 01:11:22.429
We moved in with her mother,
and she misses you.

577
01:11:23.036 --> 01:11:26.039
I miss her too.
She loves to play with Li.

578
01:11:29.385 --> 01:11:32.388
Uxbal! Hai wants to talk to you.

579
01:11:34.863 --> 01:11:37.866
See you, Lili.
- Bye. Say bye.

580
01:11:40.386 --> 01:11:42.012
Not a day longer.

581
01:11:42.081 --> 01:11:45.084
If I'd wanted them to sew 16 hours
a day and to exploit them...

582
01:11:45.821 --> 01:11:48.366
Exploit them?
- Yes, exploit them.

583
01:11:48.474 --> 01:11:51.268
Do you know what they earn in China?

584
01:11:51.387 --> 01:11:53.598
50 fucking cents a day.

585
01:11:53.692 --> 01:11:56.695
Millions of Chinese would suck my dick
every morning to stay here.

586
01:11:57.693 --> 01:12:00.654
You forget that it was I
who negotiated the workers' salaries.

587
01:12:00.780 --> 01:12:03.783
And as I can see below,
they obviously get jack shit.

588
01:12:05.737 --> 01:12:07.739
But it's none of my business.

589
01:12:07.824 --> 01:12:10.827
Just give me my share.
We'd agreed...

590
01:12:11.346 --> 01:12:13.515
Agreed what?

591
01:12:13.607 --> 01:12:15.776
Agreed what?

592
01:12:15.869 --> 01:12:17.704
You fucking asshole!

593
01:12:17.782 --> 01:12:20.451
It's my money, asshole.

594
01:12:20.564 --> 01:12:22.858
It's mine!

595
01:12:22.956 --> 01:12:25.959
It's my money, dammit!
Mine!

596
01:12:35.914 --> 01:12:37.220
Fucking leeches. If you're not
starving, it's because of me.

597
01:12:40.046 --> 01:12:42.256
If those Chinese bastards have work,
it's because of me.

598
01:12:42.350 --> 01:12:45.061
If the two of you are not sitting in jail,
it's because of me.

599
01:12:45.176 --> 01:12:48.179
If you don't give me half
of Mendoza's money, I swear...

600
01:12:49.003 --> 01:12:52.006
What will you do?
Who do you think you are?

601
01:12:52.742 --> 01:12:55.745
You twist everything
for your own benefit.

602
01:12:55.960 --> 01:12:58.963
Uxbal...

603
01:13:40.487 --> 01:13:43.490
I'll be deported tomorrow.
You have to stay here with Samuel.

604
01:13:44.749 --> 01:13:47.668
We're not staying here without you.
- Samuel is Spanish...

605
01:13:47.793 --> 01:13:50.796
He's not. Samuel is Senegalese like me.
We'll go back with you.

606
01:13:53.229 --> 01:13:56.232
We'll be united again.
We're still young.

607
01:13:57.403 --> 01:13:59.739
Stay here.

608
01:13:59.838 --> 01:14:01.714
Stay here with him
and get an education.

609
01:14:01.794 --> 01:14:04.797
Go back to work at the chicken factory.
I'll send you money.

610
01:14:06.143 --> 01:14:09.146
Even if I cut off the heads
of one million chickens--

611
01:14:10.840 --> 01:14:13.843
we'll never afford a house here.
We don't belong here.

612
01:14:14.144 --> 01:14:17.147
Why would you go back to Senegal?

613
01:14:17.406 --> 01:14:20.409
There are no jobs at all.

614
01:14:31.189 --> 01:14:34.192
A policeman came by.

615
01:14:34.538 --> 01:14:37.541
He says we'll be evicted.
All of us. We have until Monday.

616
01:14:40.277 --> 01:14:43.239
Let Uxbal handle it.

617
01:14:43.365 --> 01:14:45.575
I trust him.

618
01:14:45.670 --> 01:14:48.673
I have already spoken with him.

619
01:14:50.801 --> 01:14:53.804
Let him help us.

620
01:15:16.022 --> 01:15:18.691
Hello.

621
01:15:18.804 --> 01:15:21.807
Why do you look so sulky?
What happened to you?

622
01:15:22.456 --> 01:15:25.459
Why did you do it?
You didn't have to go that far.

623
01:15:28.110 --> 01:15:31.113
Is that why you asked me to come?
To give me an earful?

624
01:15:34.589 --> 01:15:37.592
What could I have done?
They do whatever the hell they want.

625
01:15:39.024 --> 01:15:40.776
What did you expect?

626
01:15:40.850 --> 01:15:43.853
Were you the only one who didn't know
that they sold drugs?

627
01:15:44.068 --> 01:15:47.030
I warned you, Uxbal.
We had to stop the negroes.

628
01:15:48.808 --> 01:15:51.811
There's not enough money for everyone.
Should I live on my miserable salary?

629
01:15:53.808 --> 01:15:55.935
Or would you steal from me?

630
01:15:56.026 --> 01:15:59.029
They're going to be deported.
There are women with small children...

631
01:15:59.592 --> 01:16:02.595
You damn well aren't Mother Teresa.
- You know what I mean.

632
01:16:03.071 --> 01:16:06.074
You're the one exploiting them,
so spare me the bullshit.

633
01:16:06.506 --> 01:16:09.509
I don't exploit them.
I help them find work.

634
01:16:10.724 --> 01:16:13.393
Upon payment, like everyone else.

635
01:16:13.507 --> 01:16:15.884
Would you care for anything?
-No thanks.

636
01:16:15.985 --> 01:16:18.780
Do you remember Victor, Julia's son?

637
01:16:18.899 --> 01:16:21.902
He moved to Murcia to tame
tigers in a circus. He fed them.

638
01:16:23.769 --> 01:16:26.188
They danced for him
and licked his face.

639
01:16:26.291 --> 01:16:28.836
I saw the show
with my daughter.

640
01:16:28.944 --> 01:16:31.947
She wanted a tiger to take home.
They seemed to love him.

641
01:16:34.335 --> 01:16:36.880
Just last month, I saw Victor's mother.

642
01:16:36.988 --> 01:16:39.949
One of the tigers had torn off
a piece of his face him, and killed him.

643
01:16:41.814 --> 01:16:44.817
He fed them every day.
Every day for six years.

644
01:16:46.163 --> 01:16:49.124
But he made one mistake.

645
01:16:49.859 --> 01:16:52.862
It's dangerous to rely on
a starving man.

646
01:16:53.424 --> 01:16:55.802
Let alone one whose children
are starving too.

647
01:16:55.904 --> 01:16:58.907
That has nothing to do with it.
- What are you talking about then?

648
01:16:59.513 --> 01:17:02.516
We have to help Ekweme.
He's being deported. You have to help me.

649
01:17:03.904 --> 01:17:06.907
I don't sit in parliament.
I can't help you.

650
01:17:11.862 --> 01:17:15.532
I can't fucking continue
to play United Nations.

651
01:17:12.732 --> 01:17:15.735
I have a daughter to feed.
Do you understand?

652
01:17:24.211 --> 01:17:27.214
Take care of yourself, Uxbal.

653
01:17:28.298 --> 01:17:31.301
Or take an Alka Seltzer.
Chinese food can be toxic.

654
01:17:31.429 --> 01:17:33.056
There are so many illegal workers

655
01:17:33.125 --> 01:17:36.128
--that they end up living high off the hog
while we eat rice.

656
01:18:09.261 --> 01:18:11.138
Dad, did you know--

657
01:18:11.218 --> 01:18:14.221
that when an owl dies
it spits out a fur ball?

658
01:18:15.044 --> 01:18:18.047
No, I didn't know.
Not so loud, you'll wake Mom.

659
01:18:19.479 --> 01:18:22.482
Dad, is Mom mad at us?

660
01:18:22.610 --> 01:18:25.613
No.

661
01:18:26.523 --> 01:18:28.316
Who's that?

662
01:18:28.393 --> 01:18:30.938
Your grandfather.
- Let me see.

663
01:18:31.046 --> 01:18:34.007
This was the last photo taken of him
before he left.

664
01:18:34.438 --> 01:18:37.441
My Mom always kept it in her purse.

665
01:18:38.264 --> 01:18:40.767
Where'd he go?

666
01:18:40.873 --> 01:18:42.708
To Mexico.

667
01:18:42.786 --> 01:18:45.789
He didn't travel there, he fled.
- Why did he flee?

668
01:18:46.308 --> 01:18:49.270
Because your grandfather couldn't
keep quiet.

669
01:18:49.961 --> 01:18:52.964
Back then, Franco persecuted and executed
people who couldn't keep quiet.

670
01:18:56.875 --> 01:18:59.878
When he was 20, he fled Spain
to avoid the death penalty--

671
01:19:02.050 --> 01:19:05.053
but died two weeks later
in Mexico, of pneumonia.

672
01:19:05.876 --> 01:19:08.879
Did you love him a lot?

673
01:19:11.050 --> 01:19:14.053
I didn't know him.
I never met him.

674
01:19:15.617 --> 01:19:18.620
It sucks not having a dad.

675
01:19:20.965 --> 01:19:23.968
When are we going up to see the snow?
Mom says we should go by train.

676
01:19:25.314 --> 01:19:27.691
Call the window seat.
- Okay.

677
01:19:27.792 --> 01:19:29.419
If we are going up to the snow--

678
01:19:29.488 --> 01:19:32.491
you have to start saving as much energy
as you can, because there's plenty to do.

679
01:19:33.837 --> 01:19:36.840
Now off to bed.

680
01:19:40.403 --> 01:19:43.406
Careful, it's heavy.

681
01:20:05.840 --> 01:20:08.843
Damn, it's sealed with zinc.

682
01:20:09.884 --> 01:20:12.887
Give me a hammer and chisel.

683
01:20:19.494 --> 01:20:22.080
Dammit, he's embalmed.

684
01:20:22.190 --> 01:20:23.900
We'll take it like that.

685
01:20:23.973 --> 01:20:26.976
...placed Mateo Fernandez Gama's remains--

686
01:20:27.408 --> 01:20:30.411
in Dept. 27, Saint Joseph,
the year 1966.

687
01:20:31.582 --> 01:20:34.001
Excellent. Everything's in order.

688
01:20:34.104 --> 01:20:36.106
Your father died in Mexico.

689
01:20:36.191 --> 01:20:39.194
That's why he was embalmed,
before being shipped here by boat.

690
01:20:39.888 --> 01:20:42.640
I'm telling you this because
formaldehyde might cause--

691
01:20:42.757 --> 01:20:45.135
the cremation to take longer.

692
01:20:45.237 --> 01:20:48.240
The body will be driven to
the Montjuic crematorium.

693
01:20:48.933 --> 01:20:51.936
You'll want to get an urn, I suppose.

694
01:20:54.542 --> 01:20:57.504
Here are his personal effects.
They were in the coffin.

695
01:21:00.629 --> 01:21:03.632
May we see the body?

696
01:21:03.760 --> 01:21:06.763
If you want to,
but people normally wouldn't...

697
01:21:08.805 --> 01:21:11.766
but if you want to, then I'll call
Montjuic right away.

698
01:21:18.719 --> 01:21:21.722
Tony, please open the bag,
so the deceased can be identified.

699
01:23:23.473 --> 01:23:26.393
Sorry, the door was open.

700
01:23:26.517 --> 01:23:29.520
I'll be back shortly.

701
01:23:36.258 --> 01:23:39.261
The fridge tends to hum--

702
01:23:39.824 --> 01:23:42.827
but if you whack it on the back,
it'll stop.

703
01:23:44.215 --> 01:23:46.051
There's hot water--

704
01:23:46.129 --> 01:23:49.132
but it's best that you wait
to shower until after ten o'clock. Okay?

705
01:23:50.911 --> 01:23:53.205
That's about everything.

706
01:23:53.303 --> 01:23:56.306
Kids' room.

707
01:23:57.347 --> 01:23:59.766
You can stay here, if you want.

708
01:23:59.869 --> 01:24:02.831
The rent's been paid
for the next few months.

709
01:24:13.219 --> 01:24:16.222
Damn.

710
01:24:26.264 --> 01:24:29.267
Are you...?

711
01:24:29.394 --> 01:24:32.397
Are you okay?

712
01:25:10.400 --> 01:25:13.403
I didn't know you had massage clients
in the middle of the night.

713
01:25:13.879 --> 01:25:16.507
You frightened me.

714
01:25:16.618 --> 01:25:19.162
You should see the sky.

715
01:25:19.271 --> 01:25:22.232
It's studded with stars.

716
01:25:23.750 --> 01:25:26.377
It's fucking annoying that ants
always come crawling in here.

717
01:25:26.488 --> 01:25:29.491
Ana says you caught them smoking
and that the mattress was on fire.

718
01:25:31.403 --> 01:25:34.406
Where have you been?
- Don't I get to have a little fun?

719
01:25:35.229 --> 01:25:38.107
Not with two children home alone--

720
01:25:38.230 --> 01:25:40.649
who have no idea where you are.
And dressed like that.

721
01:25:40.752 --> 01:25:43.755
So it's my fault? Now I have to
ask you for permission to be their mother.

722
01:25:44.926 --> 01:25:47.553
This is what happens
when a seven year old smokes.

723
01:25:47.665 --> 01:25:50.251
Things catch fire. Or maybe
you didn't know that Mateo smokes?

724
01:25:50.361 --> 01:25:53.364
You mustn't leave them, or throw
a burning mattress out of the window--

725
01:25:54.579 --> 01:25:57.582
and then force them to bring it
up again. He's only seven years old.

726
01:25:58.667 --> 01:26:01.670
But he can already
hurt others like he was 40.

727
01:26:04.581 --> 01:26:07.584
He wanted to open the fridge...

728
01:26:08.234 --> 01:26:11.237
and his feet were wet.

729
01:26:14.973 --> 01:26:17.976
And he called me a whore.

730
01:26:20.583 --> 01:26:23.586
The more love I give him--

731
01:26:23.888 --> 01:26:26.891
the more nasty names he calls me.

732
01:26:29.279 --> 01:26:32.282
He said it was my fault we separated.

733
01:26:33.888 --> 01:26:36.224
Did you hit him?

734
01:26:36.324 --> 01:26:39.327
No.

735
01:26:44.847 --> 01:26:47.850
Yes.

736
01:26:54.543 --> 01:26:57.546
It's the only way he'll learn.

737
01:27:12.024 --> 01:27:15.027
I bought train tickets.

738
01:27:15.807 --> 01:27:18.810
Four seats in first class.

739
01:27:19.807 --> 01:27:22.810
I found a cute guest house
where we can stay overnight.

740
01:27:25.503 --> 01:27:28.465
The kids are so looking forward
to the trip.

741
01:27:28.896 --> 01:27:31.815
They talk about the Pyrenees--

742
01:27:35.592 --> 01:27:38.428
as if we were going to Disneyland.

743
01:27:38.157 --> 01:27:41.160
Honey, what you're seeing there,
aren't stars.

744
01:27:42.419 --> 01:27:45.422
It's your nervous system.

745
01:27:48.289 --> 01:27:51.292
If you would only hold me...

746
01:28:55.993 --> 01:28:58.996
We're ruined.

747
01:29:00.994 --> 01:29:03.997
Finished.

748
01:29:04.516 --> 01:29:07.311
We could've...

749
01:29:07.430 --> 01:29:10.182
Calm down.
It was your idea.

750
01:29:10.299 --> 01:29:13.302
What happened?
Where are they?

751
01:29:13.691 --> 01:29:16.527
Where are they?
- You fucking pig!

752
01:29:16.648 --> 01:29:19.567
You're a fucking murderer.
